<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>

<section xml:id="sec_activecode_decision_tree_obstacle_sorting" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>ActiveCode Challenge: Decision Tree Classifier for Obstacle Sorting</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>In this exercise, you will build a pure Python decision tree classification loop. Standard Runestone CodeLens and ActiveCode environments do not support external libraries like <c>scikit-learn</c> or <c>opencv</c>. Therefore, you will write pure Python logic that mimics a decision tree classifier to sort data coordinates into "obstacle" or "free space".</p>
  </introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="subsec_decision_tree_obstacle_sorting_exercises">
    <title>Section 6.4 Interactive Exercises</title>

    <subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec_decision_tree_classifier_challenge">
      <title>Exercise 6.4.1: Decision Tree Classifier Challenge</title>
      <p>Complete the decision tree classifier below to sort incoming coordinate telemetry into "OBSTACLE" vs. "FREE_SPACE".</p>
      <p><term>Task:</term></p>
      <p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <p>Complete the <c>predict_decision_tree</c> function according to these decision rules:</p>
            <p>
              <ul>
                <li>If <c>x_coord &lt; 2.0</c> AND <c>y_coord &lt; 2.0</c>, classify as <c>"OBSTACLE"</c>.</li>
                <li>Otherwise, classify as <c>"FREE_SPACE"</c>.</li>
              </ul>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li><p>Run the script to evaluate the accuracy of your classifier against the test dataset!</p></li>
        </ol>
      </p>
      <program xml:id="ac_decision_tree" interactive="activecode" language="python">
        <input>
def predict_decision_tree(x_coord, y_coord):
    # TODO: Implement decision tree logic
    # Rule: If x &lt; 2.0 AND y &lt; 2.0 -&gt; return "OBSTACLE"
    # Otherwise -&gt; return "FREE_SPACE"

    predicted_label = "FREE_SPACE"
    return predicted_label

# Telemetry Test Dataset: List of ((x, y), ground_truth_label)
test_dataset = [
    ((0.5, 1.2), "OBSTACLE"),
    ((3.1, 0.8), "FREE_SPACE"),
    ((1.8, 1.9), "OBSTACLE"),
    ((2.5, 4.0), "FREE_SPACE"),
    ((0.2, 3.5), "FREE_SPACE")
]

print("--- Running Decision Tree Classifier Evaluation ---")
correct_predictions = 0

for i, (coords, true_label) in enumerate(test_dataset):
    x, y = coords
    pred_label = predict_decision_tree(x, y)

    is_correct = (pred_label == true_label)
    if is_correct:
        correct_predictions += 1

    print(f"Sample {i+1}: Coords=({x}, {y}) | True={true_label:10s} | Pred={pred_label:10s} | Match={is_correct}")

accuracy = (correct_predictions / len(test_dataset)) * 100.0
print(f"\nClassifier Accuracy: {accuracy:.1f}%")
</input>
      </program>
    </subsubsection>
  </subsection>
</section>
